            "review_title": "Review at Mama Moos",
            "review_text": "Kitch\nReading, United Kingdom87 contributions\n0\nI think they’ve given up\nJan 2018 • Friends\nWent in here last night with 2 friends. First impressions was if they were actually open, no-one inside, 3 people sat outside eating, and it looked like a few young locals were also using it as a hang-out, didn’t see them eating or drinking. Seated by very young staff, and the girls were also joined by one of the local lads from outside who stood there with his hands in his pockets, he was dressed like he was out with his mates, trainers, sports shirt etc. He didn’t say a word then wandered off outside again to his mates and looked like he was in charge of the music playing totally inappropriate music for a restaurant, obviously suiting his friends needs. Ordered prawn wrapped in bacon with carrots, didn’t taste very nice as the bacon was nearly all fat. Had Australian rib-eye for mains with chips and salad. Salad was very sweet. Steak was ok, cooked to order. During our meal we could smell an extreme herbal smell from outside, only to see hands in pocket man smoking a strange looking cigarette. I think this place supposed to be part of a chain, well if I was the area manager and I walked into this place, I would go bananas at the total lack of leadership. The staff all wear different clothes, the toilets didn’t even have any drying facilities, and it seems a youth wanders around aimlessly. Needs massive improvement.\nRead more\nWritten January 17, 2018",
